🃏 def-card-generator v2

Python script for generating printable playing cards from a sprite-based template, combining suit/rank icons with either a common front or per-suit backgrounds.

Designed for projects like custom decks, AI art series, or stylized card games.
Originally developed for the DarkEggFactory fantasy brand.

📂 Files included
File	Purpose
template/template.png	Sprite sheet (9×2) containing suit icons, ranks 2–10, J, Q, K, A, and JOKER
template/card_front.png	(Optional) Common background for all cards
template/spades_bg.png / hearts_bg.png / clubs_bg.png / diamonds_bg.png	(Optional) Per-suit backgrounds
start.py	Main script – generates the full deck into /fulldeck/
preview.py	Shuffles the generated deck randomly and creates a showcase.png image showing all cards
requirements.txt	Python dependencies (Pillow)
🚀 How to use

Install Python 3.7+ and dependencies:

pip install pillow


Prepare your template assets

Place template.png inside the template/ folder (sprite sheet with ranks & suits).

Optionally add card_front.png or per-suit {suit}_bg.png backgrounds.

Generate the deck

python start.py


All PNGs will be saved in the fulldeck/ directory.

The script outputs a standard 54-card deck (A–K in 4 suits + 2 jokers).

Create a deck preview

python preview.py


Randomizes the order of the cards and produces a showcase.png file with the entire shuffled deck in a grid layout.

✨ Features

Generates full decks (54 cards including 2 jokers)

Supports:

Common background for all cards (card_front.png)

Per-suit backgrounds ({suit}_bg.png)

Custom pip layouts for numeric ranks

Special center graphics for A, J, Q, K

Automatic resizing and positioning of icons

Deck preview tool (preview.py) for quick showcases

